#[section, $md:
    @../../ (Documentation) / @../ (Packages and dependencies) / Core packages

    # Core packages

    Core packages provide typed capabilities owned by the compiler and selected
    by the active builder. They use the same dependency syntax as source packages,
    but binding-backed implementations don't become files in your project.

    Most Core packages require explicit dependency clauses. Unlike large standard-library
    preludes, Moth exposes only a small always-available surface such as `io`.

    Builder and backend support can differ. The @../../progress/packages-and-builders
    (packages and builders progress matrix) records current package availability and
    important accepted follow-ups.

    ## Package pages

    - @./prelude (Prelude policy)
    - @./io (Core IO)
    - @./collections (Core collections)
    - @./math (Core math)
    - @./text (Core text)
    - @./random (Core random)
    - @./time (Core time)
]

